  "If you use this software or computational framework, please cite it using the metadata below." 
  type: software title: "Astrobiology-Today: High-Precision N-Body Dynamics, Thermal Perturbations, and Interstellar Trajectory Framework"
  authors: - family-names: "Sagal Andrade" given-names: "Rene" orcid: "[suspicious link removed]" affiliation: "Independent Researcher (University College London Alumnus)"
  email: "sagal233rene@outlook.com" version: "1.0.0" date-released: "2026-11-10" repository-code: "[suspicious link removed]" url: "[suspicious link removed]"
  license: MIT keywords: - "celestial mechanics" - "orbital dynamics" - "n-body simulation" - "planetary defense" - "apophis-2029" - "yarkovsky-effect" - "interstellar-comet" - "3iatlas" - "rebound-ias15" - "open-science"
  abstract: &gt;- A high-precision computational framework for celestial mechanics, planetary defense modeling, and non-gravitational thermal perturbation mapping. 
  Implements multi-body N-body numerical integration (REBOUND IAS15 / DOP853 engines) resolving the April 2029 deep geocentric flyby of asteroid (99942) Apophis (minimum perigee 36,082.12 km / 38,011.82 km), its Aten-to-Apollo orbital class mutation (a\_pre=0.9241 AU to a\_post=0.9535 AU), and sub-meter Yarkovsky thermal drift (18.0 cm). 
  Includes an adaptive RK45 hyperbolic engine validating comet 3I/ATLAS trajectory (e=6.1414, 236.36 m outgassing deflection, 50-Myr galactic origin). 
  preferred-citation: type: article authors: - family-names: "Sagal Andrade" given-names: "Rene" orcid: "[suspicious link removed]" 
  title: "High-Precision Numerical Mapping of Yarkovsky Perturbations and Non-Linear Flyby Dynamics of Asteroid (99942) Apophis in 2029"
  journal: "Astronomy and Computing" year: 2026 status: "submitted"
